WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.032 --> 00:00:01.974
- [Kelly] So well, let's talk
about "Love Is Blind" though.

00:00:01.974 --> 00:00:03.073
- Let's do it.
- Yes.

00:00:03.073 --> 00:00:04.571
- So how does this show work?

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:06.040
- Well like you said, it's
like the dating version

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:08.492
of "The Voice", so that's
all people can go off of,

00:00:08.492 --> 00:00:11.680
is they, we have 15 single
guys and 15 single girls

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:13.981
in these dating pods, and
they talk to each other,

00:00:13.981 --> 00:00:17.485
for days, weeks, with no
cell phone, no television,

00:00:17.485 --> 00:00:20.777
no computers, no family
and friends in their ear,

00:00:20.777 --> 00:00:21.677
and they just get to know each other.

00:00:21.677 --> 00:00:23.118
- [Kelly] First of all, this
just sounds like vacation.

00:00:23.118 --> 00:00:24.959
(laughs)

00:00:24.959 --> 00:00:27.034
- You know what, all they
have is communication,

00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:29.281
like the old school way of
getting to know somebody,

00:00:29.281 --> 00:00:30.800
like talking, and asking
questions about 'em.

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.179
It's not about the superficial stuff,

00:00:33.179 --> 00:00:35.367
what you look like, or what do you,

00:00:35.367 --> 00:00:36.882
it's just really about who are
you, lemme get to know you.

00:00:36.882 --> 00:00:38.876
- And it's what you look
like, not a filter (laughs).

00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:40.092
- Yeah.
- Right.

00:00:40.092 --> 00:00:42.177
- Not the picture you chose
to be your profile picture.

00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:43.387
These are all people who--
- And you showed up

00:00:43.387 --> 00:00:44.365
and they were like what?

00:00:44.365 --> 00:00:45.429
(laughing)

00:00:45.429 --> 00:00:47.459
- To some of them I'm like,
"Did he describe himself

00:00:47.459 --> 00:00:48.986
to you?" 'cause we knew
what both sexes looked like

00:00:48.986 --> 00:00:51.186
and she's like, "Yeah, he said
he looked like so-and-so."

00:00:51.186 --> 00:00:52.567
and I was like, "Hm."

00:00:52.567 --> 00:00:53.676
(audience laughs)

00:00:53.676 --> 00:00:55.724
(claps)

00:00:55.724 --> 00:00:57.749
No but honestly, people fell so in love,

00:00:57.749 --> 00:00:59.495
so quick, that when
they did see each other

00:00:59.495 --> 00:01:00.803
they were like, it's even
better than I thought

00:01:00.803 --> 00:01:03.149
and there were a couple that were like,

00:01:03.149 --> 00:01:04.226
okay, we got--

00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:06.483
okay, okay, we'll just try this.

00:01:06.483 --> 00:01:07.738
And then they'd hug and they were like

00:01:07.738 --> 00:01:08.956
okay, okay, okay.

00:01:08.956 --> 00:01:11.194
- I'm mean pretty much every
scenario you could imagine

00:01:11.194 --> 00:01:12.399
playing itself out on the show,

00:01:12.399 --> 00:01:13.257
it played itself out on
the show, it was wild.

00:01:13.257 --> 00:01:15.605
it was wild.
- Cause was ya'll worried that

00:01:15.605 --> 00:01:16.918
people wouldn't, 'cause
don't people end up

00:01:16.918 --> 00:01:18.408
getting engaged, right,
that's the whole thing, right?

00:01:18.408 --> 00:01:20.904
- So you have to purpose
to someone sight unseen

00:01:20.904 --> 00:01:22.972
and accept their proposal
without every having seen them

00:01:22.972 --> 00:01:26.184
and only after you accept do
you finally see the person

00:01:26.184 --> 00:01:28.371
you've been talking to for
hours and hours and hours.

00:01:28.371 --> 00:01:30.708
- But we didn't ask
anybody, nobody was forced

00:01:30.708 --> 00:01:32.664
to purpose, so we actually, after week one

00:01:32.664 --> 00:01:34.105
we were like if nobody purposes--

00:01:34.105 --> 00:01:34.938
- There's the show.
(laughs)

00:01:34.938 --> 00:01:36.607
- Then Netflix goes, then we have to

00:01:36.607 --> 00:01:38.050
figure out what the show is,

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:40.147
'cause then the social
experiment would be nobody

00:01:40.147 --> 00:01:42.352
found love without seeing
each other physically.

00:01:42.352 --> 00:01:45.143
Well we got plenty of proposals and again,

00:01:45.143 --> 00:01:47.433
everything you could imagine
going down, did go down.

00:01:47.433 --> 00:01:49.460
Even, well.
- It's a whole lot.

00:01:49.460 --> 00:01:50.293
You need to see it.

00:01:50.293 --> 00:01:52.808
- And you got ride of, like,
any of the uncomfortable

00:01:52.808 --> 00:01:54.392
kind of vibe 'cause when I'm
going to be meeting people

00:01:54.392 --> 00:01:55.233
it's always like, "Oh my God."

00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:56.838
Like and you're just,
you get to be yourself

00:01:56.838 --> 00:01:58.510
behind that, that's why
it's like "The Voice."

00:01:58.510 --> 00:02:00.804
- And you get away from other
people in your ear like,

00:02:00.804 --> 00:02:02.006
"What do you see in her?

00:02:02.006 --> 00:02:03.165
"Why are you talking to her?"
- Or going home

00:02:03.165 --> 00:02:04.092
and googling somebody
- You're friends

00:02:04.092 --> 00:02:04.925
or your family.

00:02:04.925 --> 00:02:07.433
- That's annoying when people, I'm like,

00:02:07.433 --> 00:02:08.338
"Did I ask you?"

00:02:08.338 --> 00:02:09.171
(laughs)

00:02:09.171 --> 00:02:11.984
- It's all about the
connection between you

00:02:11.984 --> 00:02:13.527
and the person on the
other side of that wall

00:02:13.527 --> 00:02:14.360
and the connections they formed were like,

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.912
just crazy strong and in like two days,

00:02:17.912 --> 00:02:19.837
grown mean weeping.

00:02:19.837 --> 00:02:20.737
- Tears.

00:02:20.737 --> 00:02:21.570
Just broken. It was crazy.

00:02:21.570 --> 00:02:23.607
- They're like, "She's the
one." and he's like, "Really?

00:02:23.607 --> 00:02:25.143
"This show's going to be great."

00:02:25.143 --> 00:02:25.976
(laughs)

00:02:25.976 --> 00:02:26.991
- [Kelly] Exactly.

